mpany me.\" [2062] \"I'll join in too!\" Shirokuma said happily. He said he had already eaten dinner and now just wanted to have something light, so he ordered a beer. [2063] \"Are you single?\" I asked. [2064] Shirokuma smiled bitterly, \"It's very difficult to find a life partner here, and there are no family or relatives who can introduce me.\" [2065] Shirokuma Tadashi grew up in Nagasena village, but he has suffered a series of misfortunes in recent years and has no relatives left. After graduating from the Pine Forest High School, he worked at the Pine Forest Post Office and then transferred back to his hometown, Nagasena village. He looks young, but he will be thirty in a few months. [2066] \"It's not entirely correct to say you have no relatives,\" Hijima said to Shiroku, \"Right, Shiroku?\" [2067] \"Do you mean my aunt?\" Shiroku looked a little displeased, but it didn't seem like he was really upset; it might have been intentional. [2068] \"He still has an aunt, but it seems they don't keep in touch.\" [2069] \"We don't have much of a relationship anymore. When I was a child, she came back to the hometown for two or three funerals or rituals. Even if she saw me, she probably wouldn't recognize who I am.\" [2070] \"But it's really strange that you live so close to each other.\" [2071] \"You live so close together but don't talk? Is it...your aunt lives in Mukuro Village?\" [2072] \"That's right.\" [2073] Yushi looked at Shi Mu, her eyes saying, \"You tell us!\" [2074] \"The head of Mukuro Village, Mukuro Kikuno, is my aunt.\" [2075] We all exclaimed in surprise. We never imagined that the niece of the owner of Mukuro Village, who lives so close to us, works in a small post office nearby! Is this common knowledge? [2076] \"It's not a secret. My aunt was in Sumisakura village before attending a county high school, but she decided she had to go to the city no matter what, so she went to Tokyo against her parents' wishes. She's quite free-spirited and open-minded, the kind of person who says whatever comes to mind and does whatever she wants, but it seems she's not well-liked by her younger brother and the villagers. She worked in a shoe store in Tokyo while attending a secretarial school and got her license. After that, she transferred to Mukumura Seiyu's company. Within half a year, she started dating Mukumura Seiyu and got married a year later.\" [2077] \"A sparrow turned into a phoenix!\" Wakatsuki muttered to himself. [2078] Shibuki shook his head, \"No, no. At that time, Mukumura Seiyu was just a young man starting out in Ponyville. So my aunt wasn't a sparrow turned into a phoenix. He seemed to really be in love with my aunt. I heard that Mukumura Seiyu didn't just want to become a wealthy man, but also wanted to be an art patron, so he didn't have much interest in women. He probably decided to get married because he liked my aunt.\" [2079] \"Did your aunt not know you were living here? Or did she know but never come to visit?\" Asakura asked. [2080] \"She knew! But even though she knew, they were like strangers to each other and never greeted each other. For someone who hates and abandons their family, it's not necessary to recognize their niece, right?\" [2081] Shimo also seemed not to care much about my aunt. He probably considers her to be from another world, so he does not feel any kinship. [2082] \"Let's change the topic,\" said Wakamatsu as he poured beer for Shimo. \"It's about the question I asked you when you were at work.\" [2083] \"Do I know a chubby girl?\" [2084] \"Yes. The girl's surname is Chigusa. We forgot to ask if there was a letter from her in the mail sent to Mukematsu Village.\" [2085] Oh, I forgot about that. As a postman, Shimo should know the names of all the villagers. Although he may be surprised to see the name Chigusa Yuki, he may only think that it is the same name as the recently disappeared idol singer! It would be unnatural for someone under thirty not to know the name of such a famous idol singer. Wakamatsu did not mention the full name because if Shimo did not know Yuki in Mukematsu Village, it would prevent the secret from spreading further, especially with Yae present. [2086] \"I don't think there's anyone with that name. I haven't seen any letters with that name.\" [2087] I kept staring at Shimo, but he seemed genuinely not to remember, as if he was wondering what the point of the question was. Yoshida also looked puzzled, but neither of them asked any more questions. If Shimo really didn't know, the possibility that the person who told this secret to Sagihara was Tokuhara Unjirou is even higher; but even if it was Tokuhara who said it, what then?\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 2:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:05 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \n[2600] The four victims of the perfume - the \"enigme\" and \"fauve\" in the entrance, the \"Bokushi\" on the body and belongings of the deceased Ooyama Hiroshi, and the \"Weizhi\" on the copperplate engraving that fell off the table due to collision. [2601] \"Mystery,\" \"Beast,\" \"Hokutoki,\" \"Hotta Toshio.\" [2602] I couldn't guess who would do such a thing and for what purpose. It's hard to imagine that the other party had a personal grudge against Harumi. If so, there should have been a more direct way, and it's hard to see any connection between Harumi and the objects that had the perfume poured on them. [2603] \"Is there any evidence that the crime occurred last night?\" asked Higashiyama, using the term \"crime.\" [2604] \"There was no problem until yesterday evening. Hikari and I were cleaning here, and the painting was still hanging on the wall without any damage. Since early this morning, there has been a series of commotions, and no one would have had the opportunity to do such a thing. Although it's not absolutely impossible, it's hard to imagine that someone could do this without being noticed by so many people. That's why I said the crime occurred last night. However, it might have been in the early morning, as the scent would have dissipated if it was poured in the middle of the night.\" [2605] Higashiyama silently muttered \"dawn\" and looked at the door, \"Mrs. Kousaka, the perfume called 'Hotta Toshio' was also kept in the perfumery, wasn't it? Didn't you notice it was missing?\" [2606] \"No.\" Koto looked sad. \"Although I went to the perfume room this morning, I don't know if 'Unwise Man' was still on the shelf at that time. I only remember that it was still on the shelf yesterday afternoon.\" [2607] \"I've never been to the perfume room, but the perfume bottles are lined up on the shelves, aren't they? Are all the bottles the same shape?\" [2608] \"The shapes of the bottles are not the same.\" [2609] \"So, when the bottle was taken, it left a gap like a missing tooth on the shelf?\" [2610] \"No, the bottles were arranged in a staggered manner. So even if I entered the perfume room after the thief took the bottle, I might not notice the decrease in the number of bottles if I didn't look closely.\" [2611] \"What's special about this bottle called 'Unwise Man'? Is it made with special materials?\" [2612] \"There's not much that stands out. However, 'Bokujyu' does have a high alcohol concentration. Using it on Mr. Tokuko's painting is like sacrificing it, isn't it?\" [2613] \"Maybe that's the case. So, the killer didn't like Mr. Tokuko's work. Who could it be, and why involve Ms. Hagimi's work? There are so many questions.\" [2614] \"It means... the killer had ill intentions towards both me and Mr. Tokuko, right?\" [2615] \"Perhaps the truth is not so simple.\" Fujiko Zenkou interjected. \"The victim was Kozue. We don't know who the killer is targeting. Moreover, even if the killer hated Mr. Tokuko, why did they wait until now to vent their anger on his work? He has been away from here for a year.\" [2616] No one could offer an answer. Only Jingu Sensei casually remarked, \"Maybe it was based on some reasonable idea.\" [2617] 6\n[2618] Night falls. It has been a whole day since Jingu Sensei suddenly appeared in front of me. [2619] The situation has not progressed at all. Not only do we not see any clues to solve the case, but we don't know when the bridge will be rebuilt or when the power and phone lines will be restored. The only thing worth celebrating is that the rain stopped around 6 PM. [2620] Dinner is held in candlelight. I am worried about the darkness in the corner of the room and cannot concentrate. It feels like dining surrounded by monsters! [2621] The murderer was having dinner. [2622] I casually looked at the faces around the table. Everyone was silent. These silent artists, illuminated by candlelight, looked mysterious and terrifying. Shadows flickered on their faces. While the sound of utensils clinking and the chewing sounds filled with human flavor, the murderer was also eating. [2623] - Tell me! What does your tongue taste? [2624] I couldn't feel any taste. [2625] \"The refrigerator is also out of order, which is really annoying. Fortunately, it's this season...\" Zhezi seemed to be talking to the salad, and his neighbor Zhefu responded listlessly, \"Yeah, it's November...\"\n[2626] \"Let's go to bed early tonight! I'm so tired.\" [2627] Kangensei-sensei came over to me and said, \"Is there a lock in the room? I didn't notice yesterday.\" [2628] \"No, there's none. I'm worried\u2026\"\n[2629] \"I'll move the bed to block the door for you.\" [2630] \"Thank you.\" [2631] Hokusai said after the meal, \"I'm going to play the piano.\" [2632] As I was wondering why he made such an announcement, he said, \"I want to play Beethoven's 'Funeral March' for Onizuka, to console his spirit in the afterlife.\" [2633] I see. So he wants to play a requiem instead of a vigil, huh? The proposal is good, but it seems that the light is the reason why Hokusai's face is as pale as a corpse, almost like a ghost. However, several people agreed with the idea. [2634] \"That's great! Because Onizuka always liked Beethoven.\" Tsurugi spoke up first. [2635] Nagi nodded vigorously, \"I think using music to accompany Onizuka on his journey is the best. He often openly stated that he didn't have any religious beliefs, so my poorly recited sutras might be disturbing to him!\" [2636] \"Can I listen too?\" Akane asked from the far end. [2637] Hokusai looked surprised as he lifted his head and looked at Onizuka's former fianc\u00e9e. [2638] \"Can I?\" [2639] \"Uh... Yes. Of course. If anyone else wants to listen, please come to the music room.\" [2640] \"We'll go too. Husband?\" [2641] \"Yeah.\" [2642] The couple conversed as usual, with Kikyo leading the way and Yoshino following. Jing Shen and I, along with Yuki, Uzuki, and Koto, also asked Yoshino to let us attend the concert. [2643] \"Do you want to go too, Zhi Du?\" asked Zhi Du, the silent poet with half his body leaning forward. [2644] Zhi Du picked his teeth with his little finger, \"It'll be too crowded in that room. Thanks, but no thanks!\" [2645] \"You really are peculiar,\" said Yoshino, glaring at Zhi Du. The candlelight made his cheeks look like they had been shaved off. As he narrowed his eyes, a chill ran down my spine. But Zhi Du didn't even look at Yoshino and continued to clean his teeth. [2646] \"Just bring the chairs in, and there's room for ten people. I'd like to start at 9:00. Is that okay for everyone?\" The pianist's expression softened, and he asked the crowd. [2647] \"Hmm, fine,\" Kiku placed her hand on her knee. \"Thank you, Higashiyama.\" [2648] \"You're welcome,\" Higashiyama replied with a tight-lipped smile, glancing at the clock on the wall. [2649] Eight o'clock. [2650] The pendulum swung, moving the shadow around. [2651] *\n[2652] I looked at my watch and realized it was 10 o'clock. [2653] Exhausted, I leaned back in my chair, feeling drained. [2654] \"Hokutsumi's performance was truly remarkable!\" Jang Godai spoke as if in a monologue. He, like me, was deeply immersed in the chair by the window, gazing at the garden outside. His face, though calm, showed signs of fatigue, and it was reflected in the candlelight on the piano lid. [2655] \"Yes, it seems that Matsukaze-san is very happy, and I'm relieved too. The encore of 'Parting Song' was great. Saying it was an encore seems too casual, but it was like a special performance just for us.\" [2656] \"Perhaps they would have performed an encore if the audience was different. It's not often that people from the village gather here to listen to him play.\" [2657] \"Yes, but there was once last month when Matsuzaki-san performed his own composition. Like today, many people expressed their desire to hear it, and everyone gathered here. It was a very intense piece, almost entirely in forte from beginning to end.\" [2658] \"Was Zhu Dejing there?\" [2659] \"Yes. He was the only one who didn't clap when it ended.\" [2660] \"An eccentric poet?\" [2661] The door creaked open, and we saw the eccentric poet standing at the entrance. [2662] \"What's going on? The requiem concert is over.\" [2663] \"That's why I came,\" Tetsudo said, entering and closing the door. His eyes glinted in the dim room. He stopped at the piano, extending his unshaven chin, scratching his beard occasionally. [2664] \"I came to play the piano. Even after listening to Takamizawa's performance, I couldn't give a good review. I may not play well, but I don't like that guy's Beethoven.\" [2665] Tetsudo faced the piano again, sitting down in the chair, and then opening the lid. Before I could ask what he was going to play, his fingers fell on the keys. It was the third movement of Beethoven's \"Storm.\" I remembered hearing him play it at some point. Why did he suddenly start from the third movement? I understood the reason. Everyone who likes the piano wants to play this piece. Seeing me sit up straight, Jinguji-sensei also straightened his bac