id as she stood up at the same time as Miyuki. [405] But Chiyo stopped Yuki. She motioned for Yuki, who was standing upright, to sit down, and headed towards the kitchen. \"I'll do it.\" [406] It seems there will be coffee after dinner! This means that while sipping coffee, we will listen to the announcement of important matters? [407] \"Coffee cannot be served all at once, I'll help.\" Yuki also went into the kitchen. In the entertainment industry, she should have been treated like a princess, but now she works harder than us. She often says that she is the youngest person, which is a bit ear-piercing for me who is only one year older than her. However, it is really impossible to serve coffee for eleven people including me at once. It is not often that everyone gathers in the village of Mukawa, which shows that there is really an important announcement to be made. [408] Perhaps because Yuki went to help, Hakamura also got up. Soon, the three of them brought the tray back. It took two minutes for the sugar jar and milk jug to go around, and the sound of spoons and cups touching lasted for about a minute. Then...\n[409] \"Can I have your attention, please?\" Kikuno said, her voice not much louder, and the crowd became quiet.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 9:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:05 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nAlthough her performance is convincing, her eyes are like a surveillance camera, trying to probe us. [5050] \"It seems I have to retract my earlier statement of 'going smoothly.' \" Jang Godong regretfully said. He explained the reasoning he had given me in the library again - to track Onizuka in the winding stalactite cave, it is necessary to have Ari Adele's thread, so the \"Bokujyu\" fragrance was used. The fragrance should have been sprayed on Onizuka's umbrella, and the only one who could do this is Higashiyama. If we consider this as the truth, we can explain why Onizuka's body and belongings have the scent of \"Bokujyu\" and why there is only one kind of fragrance at the entrance. [5051] \"Do you agree with this explanation?\" [5052] She answered Jingu-sensei's question with a cold smile, \"Nonsense! It's a series of excuses that lead to a big mistake! You seem to think the world is as small as a chessboard. Since the bridge over the Dragon River was still intact that night, it must have been an outsider who invaded the village and committed the crime, right? Maybe it was the post office clerk named Shibukawa who killed Kuroi, after all, he had Kuroi's ear!\" [5053] \"If Shibukawa was the murderer, he would have stayed hidden in the shade of the forest, watching when Kuroi would go to the stalactite cave. Why would he go through so much trouble to steal the fragrance from the perfume room and spray it on the umbrella? It doesn't seem like the case you think it is.\" [5054] Her lips were bitten white, \"Maybe it was someone else, or someone in this mansion. Anyway, your assumptions are too big, and I don't think the prosecutor will believe it.\" [5055] Just as Jingu-sensei was about to respond, she waved her hand impatiently, \"Never mind! Please continue under the premise that Hokuzawa killed Kuroi. If not, it seems we've reached a dead end. Your arguments may be outdated, but I'll bear with it for now, but only temporarily!\" [5056] This meeting seems to be full of difficulties. So far, she has laid down a thick veil and concealed her true identity. It's unusual for her to give up so easily, and it makes me feel like there's a thorn in my back. [5057] \"But why did Okutomi have to kill Ono? I want to ask you, why do you think Okutomi is the culprit? Can you tell me the reason?\" [5058] \"Okay, on the surface, there is no clear motive for Okutomi to kill Ono. After the incident, we discussed who would want Ono to die, and at that time, Okutomi's score was still quite low.\" [5059] \"Score?\" [5060] 