nd Higashino. [2846] Doctor Nakagawa showed his identity to Mizuno, who thanked him for his help in the case, and then turned to face us. \"Did you find the body?\" [2847] I don't know if I'm mistaken, but I feel that Mizuno's gaze is sharp. Is it because he sees us as the main suspects? Or is it because he is a detective? [2848] We answered in twos and threes: \"Yes,\" \"It's us,\" \"Yeah.\" [2849] Mizuno closed his lips and turned around, calling out to the man standing not far away, \"Group leader.\" [2850] The man who quickly walked over was Fujisaki, the deputy police officer of the Fujisaki Police Department's Investigation Department. [2851] \"Let me ask you some questions here,\" the detective said, sitting down on the chair next to him. Fujisawa and I also sat down. I compared the two detectives in front of me, and my tension eased a little. Compared to the wrinkled face of the detective, Fujisawa's face was as white and smooth as a boiled egg without its shell, and his small mouth even looked a bit cute. Rather than a country detective, he seemed more like a police officer in the central government. [2852] \"Can you introduce yourselves first?\" [2853] While the detective said this, I saw other detectives bringing the doctor to the next room. Perhaps there were some questions about the crime scene that they wanted to ask him. Yoshino stood by their seats, looking ready to act. [2854] After we introduced ourselves, the detectives wrote down the information in their notebooks. They then asked us why we were still in the area. This was a long story, so Yoshino signaled for me to explain. After getting our consent, he became the representative of the three of us. When he mentioned Professor Kurata and Mariya, the detectives wrote down their notes again. [2855] Yoshino's explanation lasted about five minutes, and the detectives never interrupted him. [2856] \"I understand,\" the swamp well nods deeply after hearing the explanation. I wonder how he would react if I asked, \"Can we go back now?\" [2857] \"Do you know the victim?\" [2858] \"His name is Shougen Nakajima, a photographer from Tokyo. We were staying at the same guesthouse.\" [2859] \"You were just staying at the same guesthouse?\" [2860] \"Yes.\" [2861] \"Did you ask Shougen-san about his purpose for coming here?\" [2862] \"Well, rather than asking, we gradually learned about it.\" After answering, Momo took a small deep breath - this was a gesture to even out his breathing before saying all the situations between him and Shougen for the past two or three days. [2863] Momo started from when we saw him trying to enter the village of Muguruma and was refused, and also mentioned when we tried to illegally enter the village of Muguruma and were driven out, when Zettou Shizuku told us about Shougen's actions, and when we questioned Shougen. He even mentioned that Chihiro Oyama is hiding in the village of Muguruma. The detectives let Momo talk for about ten minutes. [2864] \"Thank you for your clear explanation.\" [2865] After Sankai commented on it, Momo sighed. Although he had not yet unloaded the burden on his shoulders, the other party seemed to have understood it well, which relieved him a little. [2866] \"So, it seems that the villagers of Mugino village don't have much goodwill towards the deceased, and the villagers of Sumida village don't know much about him either. Hmm! Let's find out if that's really the case.\" [2867] Detective Fujisaki, who was standing next to Komuro, also nodded in agreement. [2868] \"So, it seems that you are the closest to the deceased?\" Komuro asked directly. [2869] I wanted to shake my head and deny it! They probably inferred from Oyama's words that Miyamoto and I were friends who met on our journey, despite our omission of the incident where Miyamoto pushed me down the stairs. However, the wording should have conveyed that Miyamoto and I did not have any kind of \"trust relationship\" between us. [2870] \"We can't really say we're